{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","level":2,"anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are one failure mode; the other is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"singleton"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — an entity an app holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fresh installs, two singletons have "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"([E]) -> [E]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The determinism requirement","level":2,"anchor":"The-determinism-requirement"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver must be a pure function of "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"replicated content","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"type":"text","text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"both"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rows are gone."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It must also be idempotent — ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(collapse(rows))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must keep the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"IDs as ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(rows)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This is checked with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"assert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in debug builds.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows","type":"heading","text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver’s output is read as "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each should contain"}]},{"type":"text","text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ID are all updated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"title":"EntityCollapse","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO"},"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"title":"byID(preferring:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collapses rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" down to one, keeping the winner of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"choose"},{"text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"preferring","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"title":"SwiduxPersistence","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"